yle=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Talents - Alertness 3, Athletics 3, Brawl 3, Streetwise 5, Subterfuge 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Skills - Drive 3, Larceny 4, Melee 4, Stealth 5</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Knowledge - Investigation 3 </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Background \u2013 Contacts 4, Status 1, Resources 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Merits \u2013 Ambidextrous, Language</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Clan Weakness \u2013 social stigma<br /> <br /> it might be cheating using the old Outcasts book for </span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Kineticism</span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">, but it works.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T21:57:49-08:00","id":359872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/32913-x-men-scenariao?p=359835#post359835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the anti-Supernatural perspective would actually be reasonably valid here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, even very conscientious high-Humanity vampires are going to <i>eventually</i> slip up and cause people's deaths. I think most of the valid arguments against wiping them out would involve the collateral damage of doing so rather than any moral right to continue to exist one step up the food chain from human beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T00:29:23-08:00","id":359974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/32913-x-men-scenariao?p=359858#post359858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Alucard, you seem to think <i>very</i> highly of Wolverine <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I don\u2019t see the need to make the X-men into Methuselahs, though I\u2019m guessing you went that route purely to give him that Fortitude 8 power. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Just for fun:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Disciplines:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Potence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Kineticism 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Celerity 4 </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Presence 3</span></span></span><br /> <br /> it might be cheating using the old Outcasts book for [/COLOR][/SIZE][/FONT]<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Kineticism</span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">, but it works.</span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A Methuselah? He may be 5th generation, but he was only embraced in 1890. He's Canadian and there just happens to be a 4th generation Gangrel slumbering under Vancouver. Logan's whole shtick is he's virtually unkillable and a vampire with Flesh of Marble and Repair the Undead Flesh will be very hard to kill indeed. The Daredevil merit doesn't hurt either.<br /> <br /> As for the superhuman physical stats, he's no Superman, but in the comics he compares well with Captain America and other street level supers in that area. Gave him Auspex 1 because all his senses seem unnaturally sharp.<br /> <br /> His animal form is a wolverine the size of a small black bear, but I wasn't too sure what do with his flight form. The only avian thing I can think of that relates to him is SR-71 Blackbird the X-men fly in, but a blackbird is such an non-threatening bird that it would be ridiculous. Maybe just go with the color and make him a raven?<br /> <br /> Kineticism is perfect for Gambit, but wouldn't catlike balance be a better representation of his skills than ambidextrous? 8th generation is quite unusually high for a Caitiff assuming no diablerie, but it happens, after all the Prince of Cairo is a 7th gen. Probably born in the 19th century with an accent that strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 01-05-2015, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T01:44:02-08:00","id":360016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/32913-x-men-scenariao?p=359974#post359974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A Methuselah? He may be 5th generation, but he was only embraced in 1890. He's Canadian and there just happens to be a 4th generation Gangrel slumbering under Vancouver. Logan's whole shtick is he's virtually unkillable and a vampire with Flesh of Marble and Repair the Undead Flesh will be very hard to kill indeed. The Daredevil merit doesn't hurt either.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sorry, was just using some of the book's working, where they sometimes refer to all of the 4th and 5th gens as Methuselahs. Technically incorrect, sorry again. I do get trying to make him \u201cvirtually unkillable\u201d, but you ended up with and 16 soak (damage halved on top of that) and the ability to heal agg, which pretty much makes him indestructible. Wolverine gets holes punched through him all the time. I\u2019ve seen an Elder take repeated anti-aircraft fire using that setup and remain virtually unfazed (he was tossed back quite a ways).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/32913-x-men-scenariao?p=359974#post359974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As for the superhuman physical stats, he's no Superman, but in the comics he compares well with Captain America and other street level supers in that area. Gave him Auspex 1 because all his senses seem unnaturally sharp.</div> </div> </div> </div> In theory, Captain America should just be peak human (meaning 5), but that is never really represented (peak human don't jump 10 feet into the air). I don't know, just putting Wolverine at 5th gen doesn't leave you much room to portray characters more powerful than him (in this case, possibly represented by gen). I think I would've given him a higher perception rating as well. And you can always give acute senses merits for smell and hearing (with Auspex being added on top of that possibly).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/32913-x-men-scenariao?p=359974#post359974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> His animal form is a wolverine the size of a small black bear, but I wasn't too sure what do with his flight form. The only avian thing I can think of that relates to him is SR-71 Blackbird the X-men fly in, but a blackbird is such an non-threatening bird that it would be ridiculous. Maybe just go with the color and make him a raven?</div> </div> </div> </div> I wouldn't worry so much about animal forms or the specifics of every level of each discipline. Wolverine doesn't sink into the floor either. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/32913-x-men-scenariao?p=359974#post359974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Kineticism is perfect for Gambit, but wouldn't catlike balance be a better representation of his skills than ambidextrous? 8th generation is quite unusually high for a Caitiff assuming no diablerie, but it happens, after all the Prince of Cairo is a 7th gen. Probably born in the 19th century with an accent that strong.</div> </div> </div> </div> With a Dex of 5 and 3 Athletics (I would\u2019ve added the Skill Acrobatics, but I feel V20 made most secondary skills obsolete), and 4 Celerity, I don\u2019t think any balance rolls are going to matter much. The Ambidextrous thing was just because I seem to remember Gambit being so. I\u2019m sure there are a ton of extra merits that can be added on to any representation of a comic book character that would make them better at doing heroic things. Besides, I just threw that together on lunch today at work and so didn\u2019t have any books on hand.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T08:07:21-08:00","id":360212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/32913-x-men-scenariao?p=359835#post359835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't be exactly the same situation, since in X-Men, for the most part mutants are just people trying to get by, with the prejudice being portrayed (depending on the writer) as irrational knee-jerk, or the result of a few &quot;bad&quot; mutants leading to fear of all mutants. Vampires, in contrast, actively feed on humans. Mages are basically schizophrenic, and <b>Uratha are... problematic at best, from a human point of view.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>This is the classic WoD board. We have Garou, not Uratha. Between the two, people would probably prefer to deal with Uratha, since they don't hit nearly as hard and don't have inherent super speed, and that's before you get into the underlying motivations and cosmological details that make Garou adversarial to most civilizations (however bad the Garou are presented as having done, humans always take it further and manage to do worse.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T17:43:33-08:00","id":360788,"title":"","content":"Garou. Right. I knew the CWoD Werewolves were called that, just got wires crossed for a sec. My point still stands, Garou don't exactly play well with humans either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T06:54:38-08:00","id":361261,"title":"","content":"I love the garou their holy warriors of nature.<br /> <br /> Still I liked the potential legal implications brought up in PRoject twilight<br /> <br /> &quot;Do garou violate leash laws, do blood bonds constitute slavery, if a garou kills a vampire for being &quot;of the wyrm&quot; is that a hate crime, is it even murder.?<br /> <br /> Is the erradication or even reigning in of supernatural beings even within the juridstiction of the government.<br /> <br /> The &quot;You should have reported this!&quot; argument... is cool I think as to an outsider it makes sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> IN the Gehenna book one of the groups it lists Wants Registration ... which is not an idea any supernatural except MAYBE teh Children of Gaia, will submit to.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T07:31:53-08:00","id":361282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/32913-x-men-scenariao?p=361261#post361261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the garou their holy warriors of nature.<br /> <br /> Still I liked the potential legal implications brought up in PRoject twilight<br /> <br /> &quot;Do garou violate leash laws, do blood bonds constitute slavery, if a garou kills a vampire for being &quot;of the wyrm&quot; is that a hate crime, is it even murder.?<br /> <br /> Is the erradication or even reigning in of supernatural beings even within the juridstiction of the government.<br /> <br /> The &quot;You should have reported this!&quot; argument... is cool I think as to an outsider it makes sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> IN the Gehenna book one of the groups it lists Wants Registration ... which is not an idea any supernatural except MAYBE teh Children of Gaia, will submit to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even a maybe, a definite no. The Children want the Garou and Fera to stand together unified, not to submit to a corrupt human government.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T22:05:41-08:00","id":365112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/32913-x-men-scenariao?p=360016#post360016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I do get trying to make him \u201cvirtually unkillable\u201d, but you ended up with and 16 soak (damage halved on top of that) and the ability to heal agg, which pretty much makes him indestructible. Wolverine gets holes punched through him all the time. I\u2019ve seen an Elder take repeated anti-aircraft fire using that setup and remain virtually unfazed (he was tossed back quite a ways).</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did you get the stats for an anti-aircraft gun? What kind of AA are we talking about, 37mm, 88mm, missiles?<br /> <br /> 15 soak (he gained the power, not an eighth die).<br /> <br /> He does get holes punched in him all the time in the comics and movies, and he inevitably heals unless he's vaporized. In a game with strict mechanics to how healing works that's just not going to fly, so I simply went for the way in which he could best represent his core theme, being unkillable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T23:06:41-08:00","id":365135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/32913-x-men-scenariao?p=365112#post365112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where did you get the stats for an anti-aircraft gun? What kind of AA are we talking about, 37mm, 88mm, missiles?<br /> <br /> 15 soak (he gained the power, not an eighth die).<br /> <br /> He does get holes punched in him all the time in the comics and movies, and he inevitably heals unless he's vaporized. In a game with strict mechanics to how healing works that's just not going to fly, so I simply went for the way in which he could best represent his core theme, being unkillable.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would've been years and years ago. I want to say we were using the stats for both the 120 mm gun (single shot) and the 30mm canon (going full auto). Stats were from the Vampire Players Guide. It was ruled that they did normal damage (and so were relatively easy to heal using blood). We started off testing hitting him from normal range and eventually moved up to point blank (dif 4 to hit). After several shots (4 or 5) at point blank we managed to get him to take 3 damage (maybe). I don't remember how much he had taken, I just remember that he had healed it within 1 round of spending blood. It was something ridiculous like that. The entire point of the exercise was to see how much he had to fear from modern weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T07:30:53-08:00","id":365405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/32913-x-men-scenariao?p=365135#post365135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This would've been years and years ago. I want to say we were using the stats for both the 120 mm gun (single shot) and the 30mm canon (going full auto). Stats were from the Vampire Players Guide. It was ruled that they did normal damage (and so were relatively easy to heal using blood). We started off testing hitting him from normal range and eventually moved up to point blank (dif 4 to hit). After several shots (4 or 5) at point blank we managed to get him to take 3 damage (maybe). I don't remember how much he had taken, I just remember that he had healed it within 1 round of spending blood. It was something ridiculous like that. The entire point of the exercise was to see how much he had to fear from modern weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, ran the math and 105 mm is definitely survivable, 120 mm you'll have to be lucky though. Still that's pretty incredible. <br /> <br /> Anyways, since the likelyhood of being hit directly by a tank round in most games is virtually 'nill, someone at that level is basically unstoppable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T19:02:33-08:00","id":365909,"title":"","content":"Only in roleplaying do we have people actually calculating how big a tank shell you can survive being hit by.<br /> <br /> I love this hobby. So much. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T19:25:05-08:00","id":365922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/32913-x-men-scenariao?p=365405#post365405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh, ran the math and 105 mm is definitely survivable, 120 mm you'll have to be lucky though. Still that's pretty incredible.<br /> <br /> Anyways, since the likelyhood of being hit directly by a tank round in most games is virtually 'nill, someone at that level is basically unstoppable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unstoppable? You're not using enough ordnance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T22:53:28-08:00","id":366081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/32913-x-men-scenariao?p=365909#post365909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only in roleplaying do we have people actually calculating how big a tank shell you can survive being hit by.<br /> <br /> I love this hobby. So much. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>While it was fun to roll out the numbers to see. We did come up with a real reason in game to be trying it =)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T23:47:31-08:00","id":366100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/32913-x-men-scenariao?p=365922#post365922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unstoppable? You're not using enough ordnance.</div> </div> </div> </div>How often are you going to run into a tank or have an air strike called in on you? You'd have to launch a blatant attack on a military base or run around causing havoc in a war zone. What 5th or 4th generation kindred with enough experience to build up that much fortitude and protean is going to be that reckless? <br /> <br /> A story teller can come up with any situation, but one where the above happens would have to be pretty out there. Maybe a Summerian mother/fertility goddess comes out of torpor in Iraq and flips her shit over the current situation and launches her own private one woman war against ISIS, giving no fucks about the masquerade?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T09:21:25-08:00","id":366363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/32913-x-men-scenariao?p=366100#post366100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How often are you going to run into a tank or have an air strike called in on you? You'd have to launch a blatant attack on a military base or run around causing havoc in a war zone. What 5th or 4th generation kindred with enough experience to build up that much fortitude and protean is going to be that reckless?<br /> <br /> A story teller can come up with any situation, but one where the above happens would have to be pretty out there. Maybe a Summerian mother/fertility goddess comes out of torpor in Iraq and flips her shit over the current situation and launches her own private one woman war against ISIS, giving no fucks about the masquerade?</div> </div> </div> </div>The elder might not be reckless, but humans fighting a war tend to not be mindful of the potential existence of legendary monsters or their lairs, as you seem to agree. Planning for haven security several centuries in the past can fail spectacularly when military forces decide to roll some armor on through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T16:04:53-08:00","id":366699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/32913-x-men-scenariao?p=366363#post366363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The elder might not be reckless, but humans fighting a war tend to not be mindful of the potential existence of legendary monsters or their lairs, as you seem to agree. Planning for haven security several centuries in the past can fail spectacularly when military forces decide to roll some armor on through.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they catch you asleep it hardly counts, a peasant with a torch can be dangerous to any vampire then. If he's awake, the armor rolling through should not come as a surprise. That kind of thing doesn't happen out of the blue. If he's not reckless he should leave or literally go to ground (he does have protean).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}